module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.CardinalGeneratedColimit.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.Completion.IdealPowerQuasicoherent
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGradedIdeal.SectionwiseQuotient
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.SubalgebraGeneratedByModule.Basic

/-!
# The graded ideal generated in one degree is quasi-coherent

Let `𝒜` be a quasi-coherent graded `𝒪_S`-algebra in the sense of Situation 01NN and let `ℱ` be a
quasi-coherent `𝒪_S`-submodule of one homogeneous piece `𝒜_d`. Stacks Tags 0801 and 0802 both
name the graded ideal `ℱ𝒜` it generates and the quotient `𝒜/ℱ𝒜`; the quotient is built in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/RelativeProjGradedIdeal/Quotient.lean` from quasi-coherence of the
pieces of the ideal, and **that is what this file proves**.

The route is the second of the two the `Not done here` section of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/RelativeProjGradedIdeal/Basic.lean` records, through a compatible
family of submodules of the sections over the affine opens, which avoids tensor products
altogether. Over an affine open `U` the family is the `Γ(S, U)`-span of the products `f · a` with
`f` a local section of `ℱ` and `a` one of `𝒜_m`, and
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.GabberColimit.sheafSubmodule` turns it into a subsheaf which
`…CardinalGeneratedColimit.isQuasicoherent_sheafSubmodule` says is quasi-coherent. That subsheaf
is `(ℱ𝒜)_n`: one inclusion is the universal property of the generated ideal and the other is
affine-locality of membership in a submodule.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGradedIdeal.mulSet`: the products `f · a` of a local
  section of `ℱ ⊆ 𝒜_d` with a homogeneous local section of `𝒜` of degree `m`, as a set of local
  sections of `𝒜_(d + m)`.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGradedIdeal.mulFamily`: their span over each affine open
  of the base.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGradedIdeal.mulSheafSubmodule`: the resulting subsheaf of
  `𝒜_(d + m)`.

## Main results

* `…isCompatible_mulFamily`: the family is compatible, i.e. the span over a smaller affine open is
  generated by the restrictions of the span over the larger one. This is where quasi-coherence of
  `ℱ` and of `𝒜_m` is spent, through the surjectivity half of Tag 01I9.
* `…mulSheafSubmodule_eq_generatedByDegree`: the subsheaf is `(ℱ𝒜)_(d + m)`.
* `…isQuasicoherent_generatedByDegree_of_mulFamily`: **`(ℱ𝒜)_n` is quasi-coherent, in every
  degree.**
* `…isQuasicoherentQuotPieces_gradedIdealGeneratedByDegree`: **the hypothesis
  `…IsQuasicoherentQuotPieces` is discharged for `ℱ𝒜`**, so `𝒜/ℱ𝒜` is data of Situation 01NN
  with no hypothesis beyond quasi-coherence of `ℱ`.

## Implementation notes

**The degree is carried as `d + m`, not as an `n` with `d + m = n`.** The degree equation of
`…IsGeneratedInDegree` determines `m`, and writing the target degree as `d + m` makes every
product land in the type it is stated in, so the `HEq` of that definition is discharged by `rfl`
and no transport is performed below. The statement for an arbitrary degree `n` is recovered at
the end by writing `n` as `d + (n - d)`.

**Why a compatible family rather than an image.** `(ℱ𝒜)_n` is not the image of a morphism of
sheaves of modules — the multiplication of a `SheafGradedAlgebra` is a map on *sections*,
`…RelativeProjBridge.SheafBilinearMap` — so
`AlgebraicGeometry.isQuasicoherent_imageSubmodule` does not apply to it directly. The tensor
route does apply, `…GradedAlgebraTwist.mulHom` being a morphism out of the sheafified tensor
product, but it needs the comparison of the sheafified tensor with its presheaf, which the
compatible-family route does not.

**The one input about `ℱ` that is not formal** is
`…SubalgebraGeneratedByModule.isCompatible_sections`: the sections of a quasi-coherent submodule
of a quasi-coherent module themselves form a compatible family. It is applied here to `ℱ`, and
`…GabberColimit.span_range_restrict_eq_top` to `𝒜_m`; between them they expand a product of
sections over a small affine open into a combination of restrictions of products over a larger
one, which is the whole content of compatibility.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NN)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01I9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01I9)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0801](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0801)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0802](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0802)

## Not done here

No Stacks tag is claimed. Neither Tag 0801 nor Tag 0802 is proved: what they still need is the
identification of the closed subscheme with the relative Proj of the quotient, which is not a
quasi-coherence question. See the `Not done here` sections of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/RelativeProjGradedIdeal/Quotient.lean` and
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/RelativeProjGradedIdeal/ClosedTwistAlgebra.lean`.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry TopologicalSpace Opposite
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjBridge
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.GabberColimit

universe u

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGradedIdeal

attribute [local instance_reducible] AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules

variable {S : Scheme.{u}} (𝒜 : SheafGradedAlgebra S) {d : ℤ} (ℱ : (𝒜.piece d).Submodule)

/-! ### The affine-local family of spans of products -/

/-- The products `f · a` of a local section `f` of `ℱ ⊆ 𝒜_d` over an open of the base with a
homogeneous local section `a` of `𝒜_m` over the same open, as a set of local sections of
`𝒜_(d + m)`. -/
def mulSet (m : ℤ) (U : S.Opens) : Set Γ(𝒜.piece (d + m), U) :=
  {x | ∃ f ∈ ℱ.toSubmodule.obj (op U), ∃ a : Γ(𝒜.piece m, U), x = (𝒜.mul d m).app U f a}

/-- The affine-local family `U ↦ ⟨f · a⟩` of spans of the products of the local sections of `ℱ`
with the homogeneous local sections of `𝒜` of degree `m`. -/
def mulFamily (m : ℤ) :
    ∀ U : S.affineOpens, Submodule Γ(S, U.1) Γ(𝒜.piece (d + m), U.1) :=
  fun U => Submodule.span Γ(S, U.1) (mulSet 𝒜 ℱ m U.1)

/-- The restriction of a product of a local section of `ℱ` with a homogeneous local section of
`𝒜` is again such a product: this is naturality of the multiplication together with stability of
`ℱ` under restriction. -/
theorem mulSet_restrict_mem {m : ℤ} {U W : S.Opens} (h : W ≤ U)
    {x : Γ(𝒜.piece (d + m), U)} (hx : x ∈ mulSet 𝒜 ℱ m U) :
    (𝒜.piece (d + m)).presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op x ∈ mulSet 𝒜 ℱ m W := by
  obtain ⟨f, hf, a, rfl⟩ := hx
  exact ⟨_, ℱ.toSubmodule.map_mem (homOfLE h).op hf, _, (𝒜.mul d m).naturality h f a⟩

/-- An additive map that commutes with scalars sends the span of a set into a submodule as soon
as it sends the set into it. -/
private theorem map_mem_of_mem_span {R M P : Type*} [Semiring R] [AddCommMonoid M] [Module R M]
    [AddCommMonoid P] [Module R P] (g : M →+ P) (hg : ∀ (r : R) x, g (r • x) = r • g x)
    {s : Set M} {T : Submodule R P} (hs : ∀ x ∈ s, g x ∈ T) {x : M}
    (hx : x ∈ Submodule.span R s) : g x ∈ T := by
  refine Submodule.span_induction hs (by simp) (fun x y _ _ hx hy => ?_) (fun r x _ hx => ?_) hx
  · simpa using add_mem hx hy
  · rw [hg]; exact T.smul_mem r hx

/-- The product of a section of `𝒜_d` lying in the span of the restrictions of the sections of
`ℱ` over a larger affine open with an arbitrary homogeneous local section lies in the span of the
restrictions of the products over that larger open: the second factor is expanded by the
surjectivity half of Tag 01I9. -/
private theorem mul_mem_span_of_mem_span {m : ℤ} {U W : S.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U)
    (hW : IsAffineOpen W) (h : W ≤ U) (a : Γ(𝒜.piece m, W)) {f : Γ(𝒜.piece d, W)}
    (hf : f ∈ Submodule.span Γ(S, W) ((𝒜.piece d).presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op ''
      (SubmoduleGlueOpens.sections ℱ U : Set Γ(𝒜.piece d, U)))) :
    (𝒜.mul d m).app W f a ∈ Submodule.span Γ(S, W)
      ((𝒜.piece (d + m)).presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op '' mulSet 𝒜 ℱ m U) := by
  have hmem := (span_range_restrict_eq_top (𝒜.piece m) hU hW h).ge (Submodule.mem_top (x := a))
  refine map_mem_of_mem_span (((𝒜.mul d m).app W).flip a)
    ((𝒜.mul d m).map_smul_left W · · a) (fun x hx => ?_) hf
  obtain ⟨g, hg, rfl⟩ := hx
  refine map_mem_of_mem_span ((𝒜.mul d m).app W _)
    ((𝒜.mul d m).map_smul_right W · _) (fun x hx => ?_) hmem
  obtain ⟨b, rfl⟩ := hx
  exact Submodule.subset_span
    ⟨(𝒜.mul d m).app U g b, ⟨g, hg, b, rfl⟩, (𝒜.mul d m).naturality h g b⟩

/-- **The family of spans of products is compatible.** For nested affine opens `W ≤ U` of the
base the span over `W` is generated over `Γ(S, W)` by the restrictions of the span over `U`: the
`ℱ`-factor is expanded by `…SubalgebraGeneratedByModule.isCompatible_sections` and the
`𝒜_m`-factor by the surjectivity half of Tag 01I9. -/
theorem isCompatible_mulFamily (hqc : ((ℱ.toSheafOfModules : S.Modules)).IsQuasicoherent)
    (m : ℤ) : IsCompatible (𝒜.piece (d + m)) (mulFamily 𝒜 ℱ m) := by
  refine isCompatible_span (𝒜.piece (d + m)) (fun U => mulSet 𝒜 ℱ m U.1) fun U W h => ?_
  refine le_antisymm (Submodule.span_le.2 ?_) (Submodule.span_le.2 ?_)
  · rintro x ⟨f, hf, a, rfl⟩
    refine mul_mem_span_of_mem_span 𝒜 ℱ U.2 W.2 h a ?_
    rwa [← SubalgebraGeneratedByModule.isCompatible_sections (𝒜.piece d) ℱ hqc U W h]
  · rintro - ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
    exact Submodule.subset_span (mulSet_restrict_mem 𝒜 ℱ h hx)

/-! ### The subsheaf and its identification with the generated ideal -/

/-- The subsheaf of `𝒜_(d + m)` cut out by the affine-local spans of the products: by
`mulSheafSubmodule_eq_generatedByDegree` it is `(ℱ𝒜)_(d + m)`. -/
def mulSheafSubmodule (hqc : ((ℱ.toSheafOfModules : S.Modules)).IsQuasicoherent) (m : ℤ) :
    (𝒜.piece (d + m)).Submodule :=
  sheafSubmodule (𝒜.piece (d + m)) (mulFamily 𝒜 ℱ m) (isCompatible_mulFamily 𝒜 ℱ hqc m)

/-- **The subsheaf cut out by the affine-local spans of the products is the degree-`d + m` piece
of the generated graded ideal.** One inclusion is the universal property of `ℱ𝒜`, the other is
affine-locality of membership in a submodule. -/
theorem mulSheafSubmodule_eq_generatedByDegree
    (hqc : ((ℱ.toSheafOfModules : S.Modules)).IsQuasicoherent) (m : ℤ) :
    mulSheafSubmodule 𝒜 ℱ hqc m = generatedByDegree 𝒜 ℱ (d + m) := by
  refine le_antisymm (fun X s hs => ?_) ?_
  · refine Stacks.Algebraization.mem_submodule_of_affine _ X.unop s fun V i => ?_
    have hle : mulFamily 𝒜 ℱ m V ≤
        SubmoduleGlueOpens.sections (generatedByDegree 𝒜 ℱ (d + m)) V.1 := by
      refine Submodule.span_le.2 ?_
      rintro - ⟨f, hf, a, rfl⟩
      exact isGeneratedInDegree_generatedByDegree 𝒜 ℱ (d + m) m rfl V.1 f hf a _ HEq.rfl
    exact hle (hs V i.le)
  · refine generatedByDegree_le 𝒜 ℱ fun m' hm' U f hf a x hx => ?_
    obtain rfl : m' = m := by omega
    obtain rfl := eq_of_heq hx
    intro V hVU
    exact Submodule.subset_span (mulSet_restrict_mem 𝒜 ℱ hVU ⟨f, hf, a, rfl⟩)

/-- **The degree-`n` piece of the graded ideal generated by a quasi-coherent submodule of one
homogeneous piece is quasi-coherent**, in every degree. -/
theorem isQuasicoherent_generatedByDegree_of_mulFamily
    (hqc : ((ℱ.toSheafOfModules : S.Modules)).IsQuasicoherent) (n : ℤ) :
    (((generatedByDegree 𝒜 ℱ n).toSheafOfModules : S.Modules)).IsQuasicoherent := by
  obtain ⟨m, rfl⟩ : ∃ m : ℤ, n = d + m := ⟨n - d, by omega⟩
  rw [← mulSheafSubmodule_eq_generatedByDegree 𝒜 ℱ hqc m]
  exact isQuasicoherent_sheafSubmodule (𝒜.piece (d + m)) (mulFamily 𝒜 ℱ m)
    (isCompatible_mulFamily 𝒜 ℱ hqc m)

/-- **The pieces of `𝒜/ℱ𝒜` are quasi-coherent.** This is the hypothesis
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGradedIdeal.IsQuasicoherentQuotPieces` of the quotient
construction, discharged for the graded ideal generated by a quasi-coherent submodule of one
homogeneous piece. -/
theorem isQuasicoherentQuotPieces_gradedIdealGeneratedByDegree
    (hqc : ((ℱ.toSheafOfModules : S.Modules)).IsQuasicoherent) :
    IsQuasicoherentQuotPieces 𝒜 (gradedIdealGeneratedByDegree 𝒜 ℱ) :=
  isQuasicoherentQuotPieces 𝒜 (gradedIdealGeneratedByDegree 𝒜 ℱ)
    (isQuasicoherent_generatedByDegree_of_mulFamily 𝒜 ℱ hqc)

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGradedIdeal

end
